  "text_pages": [
    "Your arrival - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nGo to content\nGo to search\nGo to menu\nYour arrival - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nShare\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nSend by Mail\nYour name\n*\nYour mail\n*\nRecipient(s)\n*\nSeparated by coma\nMessage\nImage's text\n*\nIf the image is not clear enough, you can refresh the page.\nYour arrival\nInformation session: september (1st semester) or january (2nd semester)\nYou must attend the information session held at the start of the semester (one in September and one in January). At this event, the International Relations Mobility Team will be on hand to:\nprovide you with the administrative registration pack\nadvise you on the steps you need to take at the start of and throughout your study period\nStudent Mobility Office (Pôle Mobilité)\nOur Mobility team welcomes you in the afternoon from Monday to Thursday (1:30pm-4:30pm), and on Friday morning (9am-12pm) for any queries. You can also contact the Mobility Office by mail: incomingstudents@u-bordeaux-montaigne.fr.\nIf your home university ask you to send them an attendance certificate signed at the beginning and at the end of your stay. The Mobility office will sign the document from September 1st.\nRegistration\nFor 3 weeks (until the end of september) following the orientation session, our tutors will guide you for your final registration to your classes.\nYou will receive a registration schedule by email.\nStudent ID Card (Aquipass)\nBordeaux Montaigne University  provides their international students\nwith an “Aquipass” card. This is a pass card that enables students to identify\nthemselves on campus, at the administration of their faculty, in the\nuniversity libraries, etc. In the city centre, the card will enable you to benefit\nfrom student prices, for example at the cinema, for newspaper subscriptions\nand so on.\nWith the Aquipass card, you can:\nEnter examination rooms,\nBorrow books from university libraries, known as the “BU”,\nPhotocopy and print,\nPay electronically for your meals in the university restaurants, known as\nthe “RU”,\nPay for other services provided by the CROUS. More information on\nhttp://www.izly.fr\nEmail account\nExchange students get an email account at Bordeaux Montaigne University which you have to activate first. That is the unique email address the university is going to use for all communications. Therefore, you should check the account regularly not to miss any important information.\nfooter-script"
  ],
